cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rvt-open in academic or archival work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "rvt-open: Clean-room reader and exporter for Autodesk Revit files"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/helenkwok/rvt-open"
abstract: >-
  rvt-open is an Apache-2.0 toolkit for reading and exporting Autodesk
  Revit project, family and template files (.rvt, .rfa, .rte, .rft)
  without Autodesk's software. It exports IFCX, IFC4, ThatOpen
  Fragments, OpenUSD, glTF, plan SVG and CSV schedules, as command-line
  tools, a Rust library, Python bindings and a WebAssembly package. It
  is built from public observations of the file format and is not
  affiliated with Autodesk.
keywords:
  - revit
  - rvt
  - rfa
  - bim
  - autodesk
  - ifc
  - ifcx
  - file-format
  - parser
  - rust
  - interoperability
authors:
  - name: "rvt-open contributors"
